# ${{APP_NAME}}

A Rust crate created with Code on the Go.

## Run

Tap **Run app** in the editor toolbar. It runs `cargo run`.

## Test

Tap **Run tests**. It runs `cargo test`, including the unit tests at the bottom of
`src/main.rs`.

## Format

Tap **Format code** to apply the standard Rust style with `rustfmt`.

## Project structure

```
${{APP_NAME}}/
  Cargo.toml      # package ${{CRATE_NAME}}
  src/
    main.rs       # greet, main, and unit tests
  README.md
```

This crate uses only the standard library, so it builds and runs with no network
connection. Adding a crate under `[dependencies]` needs to be online once, while
cargo downloads it.
